-- Scene 1: a secret REDACTS itself -- the value never appears in output --
  [OK] Descriptor() never carries the value
  [OK] ...a :literal source reads 'from literal', not the value
  [OK] ...its SourceLocator() is the safe '(inline)' marker, never the value
  [OK] ...it names the secret + its kind, safely
  [OK] Masked() is a fixed ASCII mask (no glyphs)
  [OK] an :env secret shows its SOURCE POINTER (var name), never a value
  [OK] SourceLocator() is the safe pointer (the env var name)

-- Scene 2: the reveal is GOVERNED -- effectful actor yes, LLM refused --
  [OK] a secret is revealable by an effectful, trusted actor
  [OK] ...NOT by an inference-only, sandboxed LLM actor
  [OK] HumanActor reveals the plaintext
  [OK] LLMActor is REFUSED -- Reveal() raises, no plaintext leaks

-- Scene 3: sources -- literal (dev), env, and file all resolve --
  [OK] an :env secret resolves the live variable (for an effectful actor)
  [OK] a :file secret resolves the file's contents (trimmed)
  [OK] IsResolvableBy() is governed too (human yes)
  [OK] ...and false for an LLM (never resolves for it)

-- Scene 4: specialisations name the KIND and add one presentation each --
  [OK] stzApiKey carries kind 'apikey'
  [OK] ...it presents as a Bearer header (governed)
  [OK] stzPassword matches the right candidate
  [OK] ...and rejects the wrong one
  [OK] ...HashedBy() is a salted Argon2id hash, never the plaintext
  [OK] ...and the hash verifies against the password
  [OK] stzDeployKey carries kind 'deploykey'
  [OK] ...KeyMaterial() is governed
  [OK] stzToken carries kind 'token'
  [OK] ...not expired before its expiry
  [OK] ...expired at/after its expiry
  [OK] ...a 0-expiry token never expires

-- Scene 5: wired into a deployment site -- the key never lands in config --
  [OK] the site holds the secret OBJECT
  [OK] AuthReference() is the redacted descriptor, not the key
  [OK] ConfigJson() serialises the DESCRIPTOR, never the key
  [OK] ...the resolved key value is NOWHERE in the config
  [OK] ResolveAuth() for an effectful actor returns the LIVE key
  [OK] ...ResolveAuth() for an LLM actor is REFUSED
  [OK] a plain ref STRING still works (back-compat, no object)
  [OK] ...ResolveAuth on a plain ref returns the ref itself

-- Scene 6: stzAuth -- authenticate PEOPLE, store only hashes --
  [OK] two users registered
  [OK] the correct password authenticates
  [OK] ...a wrong password is rejected
  [OK] ...an unknown user is rejected
  [OK] Login opens a session -- an opaque 256-bit token
  [OK] ...the session maps back to its user
  [OK] ...a bad login returns no token
  [OK] Logout ends the session
  [OK] ChangePassword requires the current one
  [OK] ...and succeeds when it is presented
  [OK] ...the new password now authenticates
  [OK] ...the old one no longer does

-- Scene 7: a session IS a stzToken -- a bearer credential that EXPIRES --
  [OK] the session is a stzToken (kind 'token')
  [OK] ...it carries a future expiry (TTL 3600s)
  [OK] ...valid just before it expires
  [OK] ...INVALID once expired -- the session dies on the clock
  [OK] ...PurgeExpiredAt drops the expired session
  [OK] a 0-TTL session never expires (opt out)

